{{Infobox government agency|agency_name=Secretariat of Culture and Social Inclusion|nativename=Secretaria de Cultura y Inclusión Social|logo=SECCIS logo.png|logo_width=250px|logo_caption=|seal=|seal_width=|seal_caption=|formed={{Start date and age|1978|3|28|df=yes}}|preceding1=|dissolved=|superseding=|jurisdiction=[[Government and politics of Balisca|Government of Balisca]]|headquarters=[[Castejón]], Balisca|coordinates=|employees=|budget=|minister1_name=[[Kun Kwang-Seok]]|minister1_pfo=Secretary of Local Culture and Social Inclusion|chief1_name=|chief1_position=|chief2_name=|chief2_position=|parent_agency=|child1_agency=|child2_agency=|website=|footnotes=[[Secretariat Council (Balisca)|List of Baliscan secretariats]]|minister2_pfo=|minister2_name=}}The '''Secretariat of Culture and Social Inclusion''' ({{Lang-bl|Secretaria de Cultura y Inclusión Social}}) is a [[Balisca|Baliscan]] [[Secretariat Council (Balisca)|secretariat]] responsible for [[W:Cultural policy|cultural policy]], regulations and other matters related to the [[W:Media (communications)|media]] and [[W:Sports|sports]], and equality and [[W:Non-discrimination|non-discrimination]]. It additionally is in charge of the confederation's museums and monuments, promoting and protecting the arts (visual, plastic, theatrical, musical, dance, architectural, literary, televisual and cinematographic), and managing the [[W:National archives|confederal archives]]. 

